              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.3: Persons carrying loads"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.283,
            0.123,
            0.884,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you now understand why it feels easier to lift a water-filled bucket with a broad handle than with a narrow handle (Fig. 6.2)? Similarly, we have seen that when people carry loads like pots or vegetable baskets on their heads, they often place a round piece of cloth under the loads (Fig. 6.3). In both cases, the objective is to reduce pressure by increasing the area over which the weight acts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.282,
            0.254,
            0.883,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pressure is defined as the force per unit area. The "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SI unit",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "force",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "newton",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and that of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "area",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "metre",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "bold",
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Therefore, the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SI unit",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pressure",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "newton/metre2 (N/m2",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "). This unit is also called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pascal",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", denoted by "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pa",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.283,
            0.329,
            0.882,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If a force of 100 N is applied on a cardboard of area 2 m"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", then the pressure applied on the cardboard will be:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.421,
            0.376,
            0.744,
            0.411
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{pressure} = \\frac{\\mathrm{Fore}}{\\mathrm{Area}} = \\frac{100\\mathrm{~N}}{2\\mathrm{~m}^2} = 50\\mathrm{~N/m}^2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.416,
            0.885,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There are many situations in daily life where pressure plays a role. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Conduct",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the activities given in Table 6.1 and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "record",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " your observations. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Explain",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " how pressure influences the mode of action undertaken for each activity."
            }
          ]
